Carafe: a thread stops at a system call when it is asked to, and WoW64 reads another thread's x86 context.
wine_nx_do_syscall checks the stop request (0031) on the way in and out: a suspend waits in the server
until it is resumed, an end request ends the thread. The x86 context of another thread is read and
written in its CPU area, which FEX needs to suspend a thread.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

